\begin_layout Description
Comprehension 1:
 There are 
\begin_inset Formula $n$
\end_inset

 biased coins and 
\begin_inset Formula $n$
\end_inset

 boxes numbered 
\begin_inset Formula $1$
\end_inset

 to 
\begin_inset Formula $n$
\end_inset

.
 The coins are tossed and each put into its corresponding box.
 For the 
\begin_inset Formula $k^{th}$
\end_inset

 coin,
 the odds in favour of appearance of head are 
\begin_inset Formula $k$
\end_inset

 and the odds against are 
\begin_inset Formula $2n-k$
\end_inset

 .
 Let 
\begin_inset Formula $E_{n}$
\end_inset

 denote the event of selecting the 
\begin_inset Formula $k^{th}$
\end_inset

 box and 
\begin_inset Formula $H$
\end_inset

 denote the event that the selected box contains a Head.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Quote
Q1:
 If 
\begin_inset Formula $P(E_{k})=c\forall k$
\end_inset

 ,
 then 
\begin_inset Formula $P\left(E_{m}|H\right)$
\end_inset

 where 
\begin_inset Formula $m\epsilon\left\{ 1,2,3,......n\right\} $
\end_inset

 is
\begin_inset Separator latexpar
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Quote
A) 
\begin_inset Formula $\dfrac{m}{n\left(n+1\right)}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Quote
B) 
\begin_inset Formula $\dfrac{2m}{n\left(n+1\right)}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Quote
C) 
\begin_inset Formula $\dfrac{c}{n+1}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Quote
D) 
\begin_inset Formula $\dfrac{2}{n+1}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Quote
Q2:
 If 
\begin_inset Formula $P\left(E_{k}\right)\propto k$
\end_inset

 for 
\begin_inset Formula $k=1,2,3........n$
\end_inset

 .
 Find 
\begin_inset Formula $P\left(H\right)$
\end_inset


\begin_inset Separator latexpar
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Quote
A) 
\begin_inset Formula $\dfrac{2n+1}{6n}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Quote
B) 
\begin_inset Formula $\dfrac{2n+1}{4n}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Quote
C) 
\begin_inset Formula $\dfrac{2}{3}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Quote
D) 
\begin_inset Formula $\dfrac{1}{3}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Quote
Q3:
 Evaluate the probability 
\begin_inset Formula $P$
\end_inset

 that only the 
\begin_inset Formula $m^{th}$
\end_inset

 box contains a head .Its value for 
\begin_inset Formula $m=3,n=5$
\end_inset

 is
